<file path="handoff/HANDOFF-content-item">
# HANDOFF — Replace `S2SContentItem` with the did:ethr-signed object

> Scope: redefine the stored content object around `did:ethr` identity and add the author-signing
> and verification methods. Read **SPEC-00** first (invariants, single-source rule). Types live in
> **SPEC-shared**. This handoff is the identity/provenance half of the Lens-replacement RFC; the
> Filecoin-storage and indexing-contract halves are tracked separately but the **append log** here
> is the contract-side contract those depend on.
>
> Status of field lists below: authored from the `S2SBody` shape (the authoritative shape on hand).
> **Confirm `S2SContentItem`'s actual field list against `shared/src/rendering/types.ts` before
> editing** — they share the identity fields but may differ elsewhere.

---

## 0. Prerequisite (do first — blocks everything)

Reconcile the existing **`S2SBody` / `bodySchema` drift** before adding anything: the duplicate
`S2SBody` definitions and the nested-vs-flat `bodySchema` mismatch (SPEC-shared flag, SPEC-00 §0
single-source rule). Editing a type that exists in two versions edits nothing reliably. Land the
canonical single definition first, *then* apply the changes below to it.

---

## 1. What's changing and why

Lens is removed. Its three jobs split: identity → `did:ethr`, storage → Filecoin (CID), feed/index
→ a contract append log. This handoff covers identity + provenance only.

Decisions already settled in discussion (carry as given):

1. **`did:ethr` is the prime identity.** One identity now — the author EOA. No parallel "Lens owner."
2. **Include the DID *and* sign over it.** A DID in a field is an unverified claim; the signature by
   that DID's key is what makes it provenance.
3. **Two signatures, two roles, two homes** (do not conflate):
   - **Author EOA signature** — provenance — lives **in the stored content item**.
   - **PKP signature** — render attestation — stays **in the rendered HTML certificate** (unchanged).
4. **Sign over the plaintext hash** (computed before encryption). This makes the author signature
   verifiable only by decryptors (author / publication owners / renderer) — that is intended; see §5
   verification audience.
5. **Object ID = digest of the canonical signed payload**, NOT the CID (CID only exists post-upload),
   NOT the bare plaintext hash (doesn't commit the author; collapses identity with version).
6. **Genesis digest = persistent document identity. Append log = version history.** Versions are
   immutable, content-addressed; the document is a stable handle (its first/genesis digest).
7. **Per-post CIDs are fine** now that the contract is the index — this **supersedes the
   single-growing-DAG** idea. Confirm that intent before deleting any DAG-assembly code.

---

## 2. The new object

The secret subset is carried as **one string** — ciphertext when encrypted, stringified JSON when
not — so there are no branch-specific field *types*, which means **no discriminated union**: the
object is one flat interface. Two principles still hold: **every public field is signed** (no
unsigned public field — it would be tamperable), and **`secret` is stored but not signed** (so
re-encryption keeps the signature valid).

```ts
// shared/src/rendering/types.ts  (canonical, single source)

type DidEthr = `did:ethr:0x${string}`;   // canonical author form, e.g. "did:ethr:0x1234…"

// the PUBLIC, queryable, SIGNED metadata (all of it is signed)
interface S2SPublicContent {
  specVersion: string;        // envelope/format version, e.g. "1" — pins canonicalization + algos (§2a)
  author: DidEthr;            // was: bare 0x address
  postType: string;           // S2S kind (post/page); NOT how to parse the body
  mediaType: string;          // how to parse the body, e.g. "text/markdown" | "text/html"
  parent: string;
  position: string;
  publication: string;
  locale: string;
  createdAt: number;          // unix seconds; this version's timestamp (last-modified = latest version's, from the log)
  base?: string;
  tags: string[];                       // public + queryable → MUST be signed
  attributes?: Record<string, unknown>; // public + queryable → MUST be signed (no `any` in a signed object)
  plaintextHash: string;      // keccak256 of the secret JSON string (computed before encryption)
}

interface S2SProof {
  type: "eip712";
  signer: `0x${string}`;      // recovered address; MUST equal the EOA in public.author
  signature: `0x${string}`;   // author EOA signature over the EIP-712 digest of S2SPublicContent
}

// the stored object — one flat shape, no union
interface S2SContentItem {
  public: S2SPublicContent;   // signed
  objectId: string;           // = EIP-712 digest of `public` (available pre-upload, pre-CID)
  proof: S2SProof;
  encryption: boolean;        // true → `secret` is ciphertext; false → `secret` is stringified JSON
  secret: string;             // ciphertext OR JSON.stringify({ title, slug, content, custom })
}
```

- **The secret subset** `{ title, slug, content, custom }` is serialized to one JSON string (`custom`
  typed `Record<string, unknown>`, not `any`). Plain post: that string is `secret`. Encrypted post:
  Lit-encrypt that string → `secret` is the ciphertext. `encryption` says which.
- **No discriminated union, no `S2SEncryptedBlob`.** Both readings of `secret` are `string`; the old
  `dataToEncryptHash` was a previous-Lit-version artifact and is gone. This retires the literal-union /
  zod-`discriminatedUnion` machinery we'd planned — a flat interface is enough now.
- **`secret` is not signed.** `plaintextHash` commits the plaintext instead, so re-encrypting (new
  key/provider) yields different `secret` bytes but the same signature still verifies.
- **`tags` / `attributes`** live in the signed `public` part. **`title`, `slug`, `content`, `custom`**
  live in the secret JSON — so a gated post's URL doesn't leak its title. Public addressing is the
  `objectId` / genesis handle; the renderer (a decryptor) reads `slug` at render time to place output.
- **`isBasedOn` removed.** Edit history is the contract append log (§4). Cross-document derivation is a
  separate, not-yet-built feature; reintroduce a derivation field deliberately when that lands.
- `id: string // Lens post ID` **removed** → `objectId` (this version) + genesis handle (the document,
  in the log §4). `modifiedDate` **dropped** — derived from the log.
- **Canonical JSON:** serialize with **JCS (RFC 8785)** wherever you hash (the secret JSON; the
  `tags`/`attributes` digest inputs), or `plaintextHash`/`objectId` won't reproduce on verify. Pinned
  by `specVersion` — see §2a.

### EIP-712 types (what gets signed)

```ts
const S2S_DOMAIN = { name: "S2S Content", version: "1", chainId: /* Base */ 8453 };

// signs the whole S2SPublicContent. Scalars inline; arrays/objects committed by keccak hash.
const S2S_TYPES = {
  S2SContent: [
    { name: "specVersion",   type: "string"  },  // "1"
    { name: "author",        type: "string"  },  // did:ethr:0x…
    { name: "plaintextHash", type: "bytes32" },   // = keccak of canonical secret JSON
    { name: "postType",      type: "string"  },
    { name: "mediaType",     type: "string"  },
    { name: "parent",        type: "string"  },
    { name: "position",      type: "string"  },
    { name: "publication",   type: "string"  },
    { name: "locale",        type: "string"  },
    { name: "createdAt",     type: "uint256" },   // unix seconds (matches the interface `number`)
    { name: "base",          type: "string"  },   // "" if absent
    { name: "tagsHash",      type: "bytes32" },   // keccak256 of canonical(tags)
    { name: "attributesHash",type: "bytes32" },   // keccak256 of canonical(attributes), 0x00… if none
  ],
};
```

Array/object public fields (`tags`, `attributes`) are committed by hash so the typed struct stays
flat — but they ARE signed, so they can't be tampered with after issuance.

EIP-712 is chosen over a raw sig so the same digest is verifiable on-chain (EIP-1271 / Safe path) if
ever needed, and `recover` gives the signer directly.

### 2a. What `specVersion` pins (write these in the spec, not as object fields)

`specVersion: "1"` fixes the rules a verifier must apply, so they can evolve without ambiguity:

- **Canonicalization:** **JCS (RFC 8785)** for every JSON that gets hashed — the secret JSON, and the
  `tags`/`attributes` inputs to their keccak digests. This is the top footgun: if signer and verifier
  serialize keys/whitespace differently, every signature fails. "Deterministic stringify" is not
  enough; name JCS.
- **Hash:** keccak256. **Signature:** EIP-712 typed data, domain above.
- A future `"2"` may change any of these; the version field is what lets a verifier pick the right set.

---

## 3. The signing method (new)

```ts
// shared — new module, e.g. shared/src/identity/sign-content.ts

async function buildSignedContentItem(
  pub: Omit<S2SPublicContent, "author" | "plaintextHash">,
  body: { title: string; slug: string; content: string; custom?: Record<string, unknown> },
  signer,                       // author EOA
  encryption: boolean,
): Promise<S2SContentItem> {
  const json          = jcs(body);                     // RFC 8785 canonical JSON (specVersion "1")
  const plaintextHash = keccak256(json);               // computed BEFORE encryption

  const publicPart: S2SPublicContent = { ...pub, author: toDidEthr(signer.address), plaintextHash };

  const objectId  = eip712Digest(S2S_DOMAIN, S2S_TYPES, publicPart);   // persistent version id, pre-CID
  const signature = await signer.signTypedData(S2S_DOMAIN, S2S_TYPES, publicPart);
  const proof: S2SProof = { type: "eip712", signer: signer.address, signature };

  const secret = encryption ? await lit.encrypt(json) : json;   // one string either way

  return { public: publicPart, objectId, proof, encryption, secret };
}
```

`plaintextHash` is over the exact `json` string; encryption (if any) wraps that same string. `secret`
holds the result; it is never part of the signed payload.

Order is load-bearing: **hash → digest(=objectId) → sign → encrypt → upload(→CID) → contract append.**
The objectId exists at sign time; the CID does not, which is exactly why the CID can't be the id.

---

## 4. Contract — append log

The contract stores, per document, an **append-only** ordered list of versions.

```
append(genesis, objectId, cid, author, proof)   // genesis == objectId for the first entry
```

- **Genesis entry** establishes the document's persistent identity and its authorizing
  `did:ethr` author.
- **Every later append re-points the document** to a new (objectId, CID) — a new signed version.
- **Latest** = last non-tombstone entry.
- **Retraction** = append a tombstone version (append-only; never delete).

### NEW INVARIANT (must be enforced or the log is forgeable)

> **INV-append:** the contract MUST gate every `append` to the genesis author (or permitted
> publication owners), verified against the same `did:ethr` identity recorded in the genesis entry.
> This is the existing author/publication gate, extended to guard appends, not only the initial
> publish.

Each version is independently self-verifying (it carries its own author EOA signature over its own
payload). The contract adds ordering, "which is latest," and a **public, decryption-free** answer to
"current version of document X, authored by whom."

---

## 5. Verification — who checks what, where

| Layer | Verifier | Needs decrypt? | Proves |
|---|---|---|---|
| On-chain record (append log) | anyone, incl. readers | **no** | who published which objectId/CID, gated to which author |
| Author EOA sig over plaintext hash | decryptors: author / publication owners / **renderer** | yes | who authored the content |
| PKP sig over rendered HTML | anyone | no | the protocol rendered this, gated; carries authorship transitively |

Two methods to add:

```ts
// renderer-side (a permitted decryptor): run before rendering
async function verifyAuthorship(item: S2SContentItem): Promise<boolean> {
  const json = item.encryption ? await lit.decrypt(item.secret) : item.secret;   // canonical JSON string
  if (keccak256(json) !== item.public.plaintextHash) return false;

  const recovered = recoverTypedData(S2S_DOMAIN, S2S_TYPES, item.public, item.proof.signature);
  return recovered === eoaOf(item.public.author) && recovered === item.proof.signer;
}

// public-side: no decryption — read the log
function resolveLatest(genesis): { objectId, cid, author } { /* read append log */ }
```

Do **not** also sign the ciphertext to chase public verifiability — redundant with the record and
binds the signature to one specific encryption. The record is the public layer.

---

## 6. Open decisions (flag, don't guess)

1. **DAG-assembly removal:** confirm the append-log-as-index supersedes the single-growing-DAG, then
   the per-publication DAG re-upload code can be retired.
2. **Cross-document derivation (deferred):** the dropped `isBasedOn` was the only thing covering
   "based on *another author's* work" (the log only covers your own versions). Reintroduce a
   derivation field when that feature is actually built — not now.
**Resolved (license):** **not in the object.** The permission model is the access gate — `encryption`
on/off plus the on-chain decrypt conditions — which already answers "who may use this." A declarative
legal license would be unenforced text sitting beside an enforced mechanism (and could contradict it,
e.g. "CC-BY" on a gated post). Access control (who can *obtain*) and usage rights (what they may *do*
after) are different axes; only the former is mechanism here. The January "permitted license" pillar
is effectively already implemented *by* the access gate. If a declarative reuse-license is ever wanted
for public content, add it as an explicitly-non-enforced, publication-level annotation — not a signed
per-item field. Bilateral deal/revenue terms remain on-chain (grant/accept + license txs) regardless.

**Resolved:** `slug` lives in the secret JSON (with `title`/`content`/`custom`), not the public part —
so a gated post's URL can't leak its title; public addressing is `objectId` / genesis handle, and the
renderer reads `slug` after decryption to place output.

---

## 7. Files to touch

- `shared/src/rendering/types.ts` — **reconcile duplicates first** (§0), then the new flat
  `S2SContentItem` (§2). No discriminated union needed.
- `shared/src/identity/sign-content.ts` — **new**, the signing method (§3).
- `shared/src/identity/verify-content.ts` — **new**, `verifyAuthorship` (§5).
- `shared/src/rendering/action-io.ts` — zod schema for `S2SContentItem` (flat: `encryption: z.boolean()`,
  `secret: z.string()`) + the new `public` / `proof` / `objectId` / `did:ethr` `author`.
- `shared/src/lit/actions/types.ts` — wherever action Input/Data carries the old `S2SBody`/`id`,
  swap to `objectId` + `did:ethr` author; the renderer action calls `verifyAuthorship` (§5).
- `protocol/actions/src/libs/helpers.ts` — `requireFields` guards for the new required fields
  (`author` as `did:ethr`, `plaintextHash`, `proof`, `objectId`).
- Publication/records contract — the append log + **INV-append** gate (§4).

## 8. Definition of done

- [ ] §0 drift reconciled; one canonical `S2SContentItem`.
- [ ] `author` is `did:ethr`; `id`(Lens post id) removed; `objectId` + `proof` present.
- [ ] One flat `S2SContentItem`: `public` + `objectId` + `proof` + `encryption: boolean` + `secret: string`. No union, no `S2SEncryptedBlob`.
- [ ] All public metadata (incl. `tags`, `attributes`) is inside the signed `public` part; **no unsigned public field**.
- [ ] `secret` is one string (ciphertext or stringified JSON); it is **not** in the signed payload.
- [ ] `buildSignedContentItem` signs the EIP-712 digest of `public`; `objectId === that digest`.
- [ ] `public` includes `specVersion`, `mediaType`; `createdAt` is unix-seconds `number` in both the interface and EIP-712 (no string/uint256 mismatch).
- [ ] `attributes` and `custom` typed `Record<string, unknown>`, not `any`.
- [ ] All hashing uses **JCS (RFC 8785)** canonical JSON; `specVersion "1"` pins JCS + keccak256 + EIP-712 (§2a).
- [ ] `plaintextHash` computed over the canonical secret JSON before encryption; signature recovers to the `author` EOA.
- [ ] Contract gates appends to the genesis author (**INV-append**); retraction = tombstone append.
- [ ] Renderer calls `verifyAuthorship` before rendering; public path reads the log without decrypt.
- [ ] No `license` field on the object (access gate is the permission model — §6); §6 open items recorded in SPEC-shared.
</file>

<file path="protocol/scripts/filecoin/check-status.ts">
/**
 * check-status.ts
 *
 * Checks whether the Filecoin storage account is fully set up for uploads.
 * Reports: session key authorisation, USDFC balance, deposit status,
 * operator approval, and connectivity.
 *
 * ## Usage
 *
 *   pnpm filecoin:check-status
 *
 * This reads the session-key.json from the plugin folder to verify the
 * session key's permissions are still valid, and reads lockup/deposit
 * state from the Filecoin Pay and Warm Storage contracts.
 */

import { Synapse, mainnet } from "@filoz/synapse-sdk";
import { privateKeyToAccount } from "viem/accounts";
import { http, formatUnits } from "viem";
import type { Hex } from "viem";
import { config } from "dotenv";
import { resolve } from "path";
import { readFileSync, existsSync } from "fs";

config({ path: resolve(process.cwd(), "../.env") });

const PAYER_KEY = process.env.PROTOCOL_PRIVATE_KEY;
const RPC_URL =
  process.env.FILECOIN_RPC_URL ||
  (process.env.VITE_DRPC_API_KEY
    ? `https://lb.drpc.live/filecoin/${process.env.VITE_DRPC_API_KEY}`
    : "https://api.node.glif.io/rpc/v1");

// Session key JSON paths
const PLUGIN_DIR = resolve(
  process.cwd(),
  "../0xobsidian/.obsidian/plugins/0xobsidian",
);
const SK_PATHS = [
  resolve(process.cwd(), "scripts/filecoin/session-key.json"),
  resolve(PLUGIN_DIR, "session-key.json"),
  resolve(PLUGIN_DIR.replace("/0xobsidian/", "/oxo-core/"), "session-key.json"),
];

async function main() {
  console.log("📋 Filecoin Storage Status Check\n");

  const payerHex = (PAYER_KEY?.startsWith("0x")
    ? PAYER_KEY
    : `0x${PAYER_KEY ?? ""}`) as Hex;

  // ── 1. Synapse connectivity ─────────────────────────────────────

  try {
    const synapse = Synapse.create({
      account: privateKeyToAccount(payerHex),
      source: "oxo-core",
      chain: mainnet,
      transport: http(RPC_URL),
    });
    console.log("✅ Synapse SDK connected to FEVM mainnet\n");

    const payerAddress = privateKeyToAccount(payerHex).address;
    console.log(`   Payer address: ${payerAddress}`);

    // ── 2. USDFC balance ──────────────────────────────────────────

    const balance = await synapse.payments.walletBalance({ token: "USDFC" });
    console.log(`   USDFC balance: ${formatUnits(balance, 18)} USDFC`);

    // ── 3. Deposit / lockup status ────────────────────────────────

    const prep = await synapse.storage.prepare({ dataSize: BigInt(1 << 20) });
    console.log(`   Deposit needed:    ${formatUnits(prep.costs.depositNeeded, 18)} USDFC`);
    console.log(`   Monthly rate:      ${formatUnits(prep.costs.rates.perMonth, 18)} USDFC/mo`);
    console.log(`   Account ready:     ${prep.costs.ready}`);
    console.log(`   Tx needed:         ${prep.transaction ? "YES — run pnpm filecoin:setup-payment" : "No — all set"}\n`);

    if (!prep.costs.ready) {
      if (prep.transaction) {
        console.log("⚠️  Account not ready. Run: pnpm filecoin:setup-payment\n");
      } else {
        console.log("❌ Account not ready and no transaction returned. Check RPC / balance.\n");
      }
    } else {
      console.log("✅ Storage account is fully set up. Authors can upload.\n");
    }
  } catch (err: any) {
    console.error(`❌ Synapse init failed: ${err.message}\n`);
  }

  // ── 4. Session key file ─────────────────────────────────────────

  let skFound = false;
  for (const p of SK_PATHS) {
    if (existsSync(p)) {
      try {
        const sk = JSON.parse(readFileSync(p, "utf-8"));
        const now = Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000);
        const expires = BigInt(sk.expiresAt ?? 0);
        const remaining = expires > BigInt(now) ? Number(expires - BigInt(now)) : 0;

        console.log(`✅ Session key found: ${p}`);
        console.log(`   Root (payer):     ${sk.rootAddress}`);
        console.log(`   Session address:  ${sk.sessionAddress}`);
        console.log(`   Expires:          ${sk.expiresAtISO ?? "unknown"}`);
        console.log(`   Remaining:        ${Math.floor(remaining / 86400)} days`);
        console.log(`   Permissions:      ${sk.permissions?.join(", ") ?? "none"}\n`);
        skFound = true;
      } catch {
        console.log(`⚠️  Session key file exists but unreadable: ${p}\n`);
      }
    }
  }

  if (!skFound) {
    console.log("⚠️  No session-key.json found in expected locations.\n");
    console.log("   Expected:");
    for (const p of SK_PATHS) console.log(`   - ${p}`);
    console.log();
  }
}

main().catch((err) => {
  console.error("❌ Fatal:", err);
  process.exit(1);
});
</file>

<file path="protocol/scripts/filecoin/fund-account.ts">
/**
 * fund-account.ts
 *
 * Deposit a fixed lump sum of USDFC into the Filecoin Pay contract so
 * authors can upload without worrying about lockup funds.
 *
 * Unlike setup-payment.ts which uses prepare() (data-size-based), this
 * deposits exactly N USDFC (default: 6) directly via
 * synapse.payments.deposit().
 *
 * ## Usage
 *
 *   pnpm filecoin:fund-account           # deposit 6 USDFC
 *   pnpm filecoin:fund-account 10        # deposit 10 USDFC
 */

import { Synapse, mainnet, TOKENS } from "@filoz/synapse-sdk";
import { privateKeyToAccount } from "viem/accounts";
import { http, formatUnits, parseUnits } from "viem";
import type { Hex } from "viem";
import { config } from "dotenv";
import { resolve } from "path";

config({ path: resolve(process.cwd(), "../.env") });

const PAYER_KEY = process.env.PROTOCOL_PRIVATE_KEY;
const RPC_URL =
  process.env.FILECOIN_RPC_URL ||
  (process.env.VITE_DRPC_API_KEY
    ? `https://lb.drpc.live/filecoin/${process.env.VITE_DRPC_API_KEY}`
    : "https://api.node.glif.io/rpc/v1");

const DEPOSIT_USDFC = Number(process.argv[2] || "6"); // CLI: default 6 UDSFC

async function main() {
  if (!PAYER_KEY) {
    console.error(
      "❌ PROTOCOL_PRIVATE_KEY not set in ../.env\n" +
        "   Add it: PROTOCOL_PRIVATE_KEY=0x<your-funded-wallet>",
    );
    process.exit(1);
  }

  const payerHex = (PAYER_KEY.startsWith("0x")
    ? PAYER_KEY
    : `0x${PAYER_KEY}`) as Hex;

  console.log("💰 Filecoin Account Fund\n");
  console.log(`   RPC:   ${RPC_URL}`);
  console.log(`   Amount: ${DEPOSIT_USDFC} USDFC`);

  const synapse = Synapse.create({
    account: privateKeyToAccount(payerHex),
    source: "oxo-core",
    chain: mainnet,
    transport: http(RPC_URL),
  });

  const payerAddress = privateKeyToAccount(payerHex).address;
  console.log(`   Payer: ${payerAddress}\n`);

  // ── Check current wallet balance ────────────────────────────────

  const balance = await synapse.payments.walletBalance({
    token: TOKENS.USDFC,
  });
  const formatted = formatUnits(balance, 18);
  console.log(`   Wallet balance: ${formatted} USDFC`);

  const depositAmount = parseUnits(DEPOSIT_USDFC.toString(), 18);

  if (balance < depositAmount) {
    console.error(
      `❌ Insufficient USDFC: need ${DEPOSIT_USDFC}, have ${formatted}`,
    );
    process.exit(1);
  }

  const walletAfter = formatUnits(balance - depositAmount, 18);

  console.log(`   Depositing:     ${DEPOSIT_USDFC} USDFC (${depositAmount} wei)`);
  console.log(`   Wallet after:   ${walletAfter} USDFC\n`);

  // ── Execute deposit ─────────────────────────────────────────────

  console.log("⏳ Depositing...");

  const txHash = await synapse.payments.deposit({
    amount: depositAmount,
    token: TOKENS.USDFC,
    onApprovalTransaction: (hash: string) => {
      console.log(`   Approval tx: ${hash}`);
    },
    onDepositStarting: () => {
      console.log("   Deposit tx submitted...");
    },
  });

  console.log(`\n✅ Deposit complete!`);
  console.log(`   Tx: ${txHash}`);
  console.log(`\n   Deposited ${DEPOSIT_USDFC} USDFC — should cover many uploads.`);
  console.log("   Run pnpm filecoin:check-status to verify.");
}

main().catch((err) => {
  console.error("❌ Fatal:", err);
  process.exit(1);
});
</file>

<file path="protocol/scripts/filecoin/retrieve-test.ts">
/**
 * retrieve-test.ts
 *
 * Test Filecoin retrieval for a specific PieceCID and show deal context.
 *
 * Usage:
 *   tsx ./scripts/filecoin/retrieve-test.ts <pieceCid>
 *
 * Example:
 *   tsx ./scripts/filecoin/retrieve-test.ts bafkzcibdt4damuikjijbo5k3ramhqycdgkswqkqjftkl2xp4en3bb6v6jmsbcvry
 */

import { Synapse, mainnet, TOKENS } from "@filoz/synapse-sdk";
import { privateKeyToAccount } from "viem/accounts";
import { http, formatUnits } from "viem";
import type { Hex } from "viem";
import { config } from "dotenv";
import { resolve } from "path";

config({ path: resolve(process.cwd(), "../.env") });

const PAYER_KEY = process.env.PROTOCOL_PRIVATE_KEY;
const PIECE_CID = process.argv[2];

const RPC_URL =
  process.env.FILECOIN_RPC_URL ||
  (process.env.VITE_DRPC_API_KEY
    ? `https://lb.drpc.live/filecoin/${process.env.VITE_DRPC_API_KEY}`
    : "https://api.node.glif.io/rpc/v1");

async function main() {
  if (!PAYER_KEY) {
    console.error("❌ PROTOCOL_PRIVATE_KEY not set in ../.env");
    process.exit(1);
  }
  if (!PIECE_CID) {
    console.error("❌ Pass a PieceCID: tsx retrieve-test.ts bafkzcib...");
    process.exit(1);
  }

  const payerHex = (PAYER_KEY.startsWith("0x") ? PAYER_KEY : `0x${PAYER_KEY}`) as Hex;

  const synapse = Synapse.create({
    account: privateKeyToAccount(payerHex),
    source: "oxo-core",
    chain: mainnet,
    transport: http(RPC_URL),
  });

  console.log("🔍 Filecoin Retrieval Test\n");
  console.log(`   PieceCID: ${PIECE_CID}\n`);

  // ── 1. Try downloading from Filecoin ─────────────────────────────

  console.log("⏳ Retrieving from Filecoin SPs...");
  console.time("retrieve");

  try {
    const bytes: Uint8Array = await synapse.storage.download({
      pieceCid: PIECE_CID,
    });
    console.timeEnd("retrieve");

    const text = new TextDecoder().decode(bytes);
    const data = JSON.parse(text);

    console.log(`\n✅ Retrieved!`);
    console.log(`   Size: ${bytes.length} bytes`);

    // Show content metadata (not full body — just titles etc.)
    if (data.objectId) console.log(`   ObjectId: ${data.objectId}`);
    if (data.public?.title) console.log(`   Title: ${data.public.title}`);
    if (data.public?.author) console.log(`   Author: ${data.public.author}`);
    if (data.public?.postType) console.log(`   Type: ${data.public.postType}`);

  } catch (err) {
    console.timeEnd("retrieve");
    console.error(`\n❌ Retrieval failed: ${err}`);
  }

  // ── 2. Show provider and pricing context ─────────────────────────

  console.log(`\n--- Storage Context ---\n`);

  const info = await synapse.storage.getStorageInfo();

  console.log(`Approved providers:`);
  for (const p of info.providers) {
    console.log(`   ${p.name ?? "unknown"} (ID: ${p.providerId})`);
    console.log(`      Address: ${p.serviceProvider}`);
    if (p.pdp?.serviceURL) console.log(`      PDP URL: ${p.pdp.serviceURL}`);
  }

  console.log(`\nPricing (per TiB / month):`);
  console.log(`   No CDN: ${formatUnits(info.pricing.noCDN.perTiBPerMonth, 18)} USDFC`);
  console.log(`   With CDN: ${formatUnits(info.pricing.withCDN.perTiBPerMonth, 18)} USDFC`);

  console.log(`\nYour deposit / allowance:`);
  if (info.allowances) {
    console.log(`   Rate used:    ${formatUnits(info.allowances.rateUsed ?? 0n, 18)} USDFC/mo`);
    console.log(`   Rate limit:   ${formatUnits(info.allowances.rateAllowance ?? 0n, 18)} USDFC/mo`);
    console.log(`   Lockup used:  ${formatUnits(info.allowances.lockupUsed ?? 0n, 18)} USDFC`);
    console.log(`   Lockup limit: ${formatUnits(info.allowances.lockupAllowance ?? 0n, 18)} USDFC`);
  }

  console.log(`\n   Your piece (1233 bytes) cost at ${formatUnits(info.pricing.noCDN.perTiBPerMonth, 18)} USDFC/TiB/mo:`);
  const costPerMonth = info.pricing.noCDN.perTiBPerMonth * BigInt(1233) / (BigInt(1) << BigInt(40));
  // This is ₿ tiny — 1233 bytes out of 1 TiB (1,099,511,627,776 bytes)
  console.log(`   ~${formatUnits(costPerMonth, 18)} USDFC/mo for this piece`);
}

main().catch((err) => {
  console.error("❌ Fatal:", err);
  process.exit(1);
});
</file>

